<?xml version="1.0"?>
<OriginStorage FileEnable="1" Position="1" version="1"><popup text="PXRD" tag="" wndType=" "><popup text="Import Patterns" tag=""><item><LT>run -pyf PXRD_checkVersion.py;
import_patterns -d;</LT><LTEnable/><tlb/><Prompt>Opens the custom dialog to edit parameters, or to save/load your own preset themes.</Prompt><menutext>Full Dialog...</menutext></item><item><LT>run -pyf PXRD_checkVersion.py;
import_patterns -t &quot;Last used&quot;;</LT><LTEnable/><tlb/><Prompt><![CDATA[ Without opening the dialog, executes the last used set of import settings. Re-prompts for file selection.]]></Prompt><menutext>&lt;Last used&gt;</menutext></item><item><LT><![CDATA[run -pyf PXRD_checkVersion.py;
import_patterns -t "CIF_CuKa"]]></LT><LTEnable/><tlb/><Prompt>Without opening the dialog, imports with preset settings for Cu-Ka splitting (2θ 3-90°, step size 0.02°). Re-prompts for file selection.</Prompt><menutext>CIF Patterns (CuKa Defaults)</menutext></item><item><LT><![CDATA[run -pyf PXRD_checkVersion.py;
import_patterns -t "CIF_11-ID-C"]]></LT><LTEnable/><tlb/><Prompt>Without opening the dialog, imports with preset settings to match 11-ID-C. 2θ range and step size are similar to in-situ values, and peak shape parameters were estimated by Rietveld analysis. Re-prompts for file selection.</Prompt><menutext>CIF Patterns (11-ID-C March 2026)</menutext></item><item><LT><![CDATA[run -pyf PXRD_checkVersion.py;
import_patterns -t "Rigaku RAS Patterns"]]></LT><LTEnable/><tlb/><Prompt>Without opening the dialog, imports with preset settings for experimental patterns from the Rigaku Miniflex. Re-prompts for file selection.</Prompt><menutext>Experimental Patterns (*.ras)</menutext></item></popup><popup text="Transform Columns" tag="" wndType="W"><popup text="Add Q Columns" tag="" wndType="W"><item><LT><![CDATA[run -pyf PXRD_qSpace.py "all_deg"]]></LT><LTEnable/><tlb/><Prompt>Calculate Q values with specified wavelength for any column with &quot;deg&quot; as units (Assumes 2theta)</Prompt><menutext>All &quot;deg&quot;</menutext></item><item><LT><![CDATA[run -pyf PXRD_qSpace.py "selected"]]></LT><LTEnable/><tlb/><Prompt>Calculate Q values with specified wavelength for currently selected columns (Assumes 2theta)</Prompt><menutext>Selected Columns</menutext></item></popup><popup text="Rescale Columns" tag="" wndType="W"><item><LT>run -pyf PXRD_transform.py &quot;au&quot; &quot;scale&quot;</LT><LTEnable><![CDATA[]]></LTEnable><tlb/><Prompt>Adds a column with a custom scale factor for every column with units &quot;AU&quot;</Prompt><menutext>All &quot;AU&quot;</menutext></item><item><LT>run -pyf PXRD_transform.py &quot;gui&quot; &quot;scale&quot;</LT><LTEnable/><tlb/><Prompt>Adds a column with a custom scale factor for every selected column.</Prompt><menutext>Selected Columns</menutext></item></popup><popup text="Square Columns" tag=""><item><LT>run -pyf PXRD_transform.py &quot;au&quot; &quot;square&quot;;</LT><LTEnable/><tlb/><Prompt>Adds a column with intensity squared for every column with units &quot;AU&quot;</Prompt><menutext>All &quot;AU&quot;</menutext></item><item><LT><![CDATA[run -pyf PXRD_transform.py "gui" "square";]]></LT><LTEnable/><tlb/><Prompt>Adds a column with a intensity squared for every selected column.</Prompt><menutext>Selected Columns</menutext></item></popup><popup text="Sqrt Columns" tag=""><item><LT>run -pyf PXRD_transform.py &quot;au&quot; &quot;sqrt&quot;;</LT><LTEnable/><tlb/><Prompt>Adds a column with sqrt[Intensity] for every column with units &quot;AU&quot;</Prompt><menutext>All &quot;AU&quot;</menutext></item><item><LT><![CDATA[run -pyf PXRD_transform.py "gui" "sqrt";]]></LT><LTEnable/><tlb/><Prompt>Adds a column with sqrt[Intensity] for every selected column.</Prompt><menutext>Selected Columns</menutext></item></popup></popup><popup text="In-Situ Processing" tag=""><item><LT>run -pyf PXRD_checkVersion.py;
run -pyf PXRD_process11ID.py;</LT><LTEnable><![CDATA[]]></LTEnable><tlb/><Prompt><![CDATA[Pull all powder patterns in a sample folder and attach the corresponding temperature as a "Temp" row at the top. Only available if you selected this option during install.]]></Prompt><menutext>11-ID-C (March 2026)</menutext></item></popup><item><LT>run -e notepad %YPXRD_versionTag.txt;</LT><LTEnable/><tlb/><Prompt><![CDATA[Open the document containing the installed version tag for the PXRD plugin.]]></Prompt><menutext>View Plugin Version</menutext></item></popup><popup text="Annealing Profiles" tag=""><item><LT><![CDATA[run -pyf PXRD_anneal.py "template";
]]></LT><LTEnable/><tlb/><Prompt>Generates a worksheet template to generate annealing diagrams or get furnace settings from calibration data.</Prompt><menutext>Get Annealing Template</menutext></item><popup text="Generate Diagram" tag="" wndType="W"><item><LT>run -pyf PXRD_checkVersion.py;
anneal_diagram -d;</LT><LTEnable/><tlb/><Prompt><![CDATA[Set parameters or open your own theme to generate an annealing diagram from the current worksheet. Recommended to use with generated template worksheet.]]></Prompt><menutext>Full Dialog...</menutext></item><item><LT>run -pyf PXRD_checkVersion.py;
anneal_diagram</LT><LTEnable/><tlb/><Prompt>Generate an annealing diagram from the current worksheet using default settings. Recommended to use with generated template worksheet.</Prompt><menutext>&lt;Default&gt;</menutext></item><item><LT>run -pyf PXRD_checkVersion.py;
anneal_diagram -t &quot;Last used&quot;;</LT><LTEnable/><tlb/><Prompt>Generate an annealing diagram from the current worksheet using the last used settings. Recommended to use with generated template worksheet.</Prompt><menutext>&lt;Last Used&gt;</menutext></item></popup><item><LT>run -pyf PXRD_editFurnace.py &quot;empty&quot;</LT><LTEnable/><tlb/><Prompt>Opens a worksheet to load, edit, or add furnace calibration data.</Prompt><menutext>New/Edit Furnace</menutext></item></popup></OriginStorage>